Crosswalk 20x (ccf/fedramp20x/crosswalk.py)

Portions of ccf/fedramp20x/crosswalk.py are a Python port of the crosswalk
and vulnerability-register logic in Crosswalk 20x
(https://github.com/Mycroft-io/crosswalk-rev5-to-20x, v1.0.0, commit f2a6ebb),
Copyright 2026 Mycroft Technologies Inc., licensed under the Apache License,
Version 2.0 (https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0). The port changes
the coverage states (a "Partly reported" state is added and "Traced" is
narrowed) and the register merge (observations are ordered by document date).

FedRAMP data bundled with this product is public domain (US government work;
CC0 1.0 worldwide): the Consolidated Rules for 2026 (ccf/fedramp20x/rules_data),
the CR26 JSON schemas (ccf/cr26/schemas), FedRAMP's agency control guidance
(ccf/fedramp20x/guidance_data, from FedRAMP/JSONViewer) and FedRAMP's sample
certification package used as a test fixture (tests/fixtures/cr26_sample).
